>>
>> The AS turns on but no video signal, this time i have replaced video
>> card with no success, can you explain me a little more how to get
>> conected to the com port, because i have already conect a pc with
>> terminal emulator 9600 bps, 8 data bits, none parity, 1 stop bit, none
>> flow control, but nothing appears.
>>
>> any more ideas i wil appreciate.
> 
> Hi,
> 
> the general rule is that the default console is set to serial as soon
> as no keyboard and/or vid card are plugged in. The com specs seem sane.
> 
> Are you sure it's not dead? Battery might be a culprit too (at least it
> is for my Multia).
> 
> regards,
> 
> Marc


Quite correct. The default is to revert to the serial console (port 1, 
aka COM1) if there is no keyboard attached.

If the AS255 doesn't emit any beep codes, it should be all right.

There is also a diagnostics LED on the motherboard. It will illuminate 
when the system is powered on and it goes off when the primary self test 
is passed. If it stays on continuously, there is a hardware failure on 
the motherboard or CPU.

The battery affects only the settings saved in nvram.

When you have tested the terminal emulator, have you tried to press 
enter after two or three minutes after you have applied the power? You 
should get the console prompt if the self tests have passed.


Regards,

Kari


