Bear in mind that in boxes of this era and for some years before, the
Qbus was only used for relatively low speed IO, not just for VAXes but
on PDP11s too. Anything needing decent performance (memory, disk, etc)
was either directly on the CPU board or connected to the CPU board via
a 'fast' private interconnect, so these things weren't necessarily
limited to Qbus speeds. Having Qbus slots for "legacy" IO was
important to a lot of folks at that time.


